with witness reports isolating its origin to somewhere near Glendonald Road and Jelloph's Outlet, around four kilometers southeast of Churchill's Town Centre. Local wildfire investigator from the Department of Sustainability and Environment, Ross Pridgen, had examined the scene the day after the blaze. First responders had reported two parallel fires burning in the area before they connected into one catastrophic inferno. Pridgen was able to isolate exactly where the two fires had met, and after inspecting the location for an hour,

