00:37:44.000 --> 00:38:21.000
he had calculated the origin point for each. They had ignited 100 metres apart on either side of Jelloph's Outlet. The first started amongst the dry brush and bracken within the surrounding plantation. The second had arisen from a pile of discarded junk that included old tyres, mattresses and faulty bicycles, none of which were capable of self-igniting. All scenarios, including that the fires had been caused by car exhausts, campfires, broken glass, lightning strikes or discarded cigarettes,

