from a disadvantaged background, exhibit poor social skills and have a family history marred with abuse and or addiction. Deliberately lit fires are more common in semi-rural bushland regions such as those within the Latrobe Valley where public transport was poor, incomes were low, youth unemployment was high and child abuse and neglect occurred at a higher rate per capita. Motive could have ranged from an act of revenge to a targeted attack or a random opportunity.

